      "derivation": "The framing rule of src/gltf/Framing.h, quoted so the runner can refuse a mismatch rather than trust it. World bounds [-1.2521400451660156, -0.0005402960232459009, -0.3413881063461304] to [1.1625219583511353, 1.834357023239136, 0.25572049617767334], so centre = [-0.044809043407440186, 0.916908363607945, -0.04283380508422854] and radius = 1.5454756101823208 m. yfov = 2*atan(12/50) from a 50 mm lens on a 24 mm sensor height at sensor_fit VERTICAL. distance = radius / sin(yfov/2) / 0.6 = 11.037237418974481, and the eye is centre + (cos20*cos35, sin20, cos20*sin35) * distance. clipStart is distance - radius and clipEnd is distance + radius.",
